{"step_index":1439,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T14:33:30Z","input_tokens":2810,"cache_read_tokens":113907,"output_tokens":4169,"thinking":"Adding the interactive prediction card rendering to the teaching area is the next logical step, specifically incorporating it within the second rendering area. This placement sets the stage for the interactive learning phase. Afterwards, careful verification of the implementation will commence to ensure its correct functionality.\n\n\nNow, the interactive prediction card will be rendered based on the provided data, ensuring it's either hidden or displayed depending on prediction mode and question availability.  The display logic incorporates both the question and answer choices, dynamically generating the HTML for each choice button, including feedback on correctness if an answer has already been submitted. Further, the correct answer feedback will be integrated into a result box with an appropriate header and styling based on whether the previous answer was correct or incorrect.\n\n\nThe prediction card's HTML will be dynamically generated based on the provided data, incorporating question text, answer choices, and an optional result box.  The result box's styling and header will adapt depending on the user's previous answer (correct, incorrect, or revealed). Logic will be included to handle user interaction with choice buttons, triggering appropriate actions based on the selected answer.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Call renderInteractivePredictCard in renderArea2Teaching and implement the method","EndLine":988,"Instruction":"Call renderInteractivePredictCard and define renderInteractivePredictCard before renderLoopReturnBanner","ReplacementContent":"    this.teachStepTitle.textContent = lesson.title || step.teacherLesson.title;\n    this.teachCodeBox.innerHTML = this.highlightPythonSyntax(lesson.codeSnippe